The '''Eastern ridge''' was a long, narrow [[mountain]] range located on the [[Outer Rim Territories]] [[planet]] [[Serenno]].<ref name="Ruins" /> Opposite the mountain range was [[Serenno City]], within view of [[Castle Serenno]]<ref name="Spoils">{{TBB|Spoils of War}}</ref> and near the [[Upper forest region]] of the planet where a [[Romar Adell's domicile|house]] was situated by [[19 BBY]]. In 19 BBY, members of [[Clone Force 99]] landed at the eastern ridge in the [[Marauder (Omicron-class)|Marauder]] to avoid detection by [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] forces. They later trekked through the mountain range to Castle Serenno where they attempted to steal [[Dooku's war chest]] that was being shipped offworld by the Galactic Empire. The raid failed however and led to [[Wrecker]] and [[Hunter]] escaping into the nearby Serenno City ruins while [[Tech]], [[Echo]] and [[Omega]] sought shelter in Romar Adell's domicile. Wrecker and Hunter later managed to punch through the city perimeter set by [[Clone Captain]] [[Wilco's company]] and escaped to the eastern ridge where the Marauder was. They later left the ridge in the Marauder.<ref name="Ruins" />

==Behind the scenes==
The Eastern ridge first appeared in the ''[[Star Wars: The Bad Batch]]'' [[The Bad Batch Season 2|Season 2]] episode "[[Spoils of War]]"<ref name="Spoils" /> which released on [[January 4]], [[2023]].<ref name="Airdate">{{SW|url=news/star-wars-the-bad-batch-season-2-trailer-key-art|text=Clone Force 99 Is Back in New ''Star Wars: The Bad Batch'' Season 2 Trailer}}</ref> It was later identified in the episode "[[Ruins of War]]"<ref name="Ruins" /> which was released on the same date.<ref name="Airdate" />

